# Text Rune compiles in, hashes or runs is LF in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says: the
# precompiled shaders are keyed to the WGSL's bytes (crates/rune/build.rs also reads CRLF as LF,
# for checkouts made before this file), and a shell script with CRLF doesn't run.
*.wgsl text eol=lf
*.luau text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.mmd text eol=lf
*.vert text eol=lf
*.frag text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
# The vendored wgpu-hal and its patch, byte for byte as committed in every checkout: the crate as
# published has a CRLF file among its LF ones, and scripts/vendor-wgpu-hal.sh --regenerate diffs the
# source against it, so a converting checkout would write a whole-file patch.
vendor/wgpu-hal/** -text
*.patch -text

# Precompiled shaders and raw pixel data, never converted.
*.dxbc binary
*.metallib binary
*.rgba binary
*.bin binary
